SUMMARY {"label": "W9-L-llamacpp-r1", "load_s": 34.0, "vram_idle_mib": 14207, "vram_peak_mib": 14775, "rows": [{"depth": 1055, "prompt_n": 1055, "prefill_tps": 625.8, "decode_tps": 37.97, "decode_ms": 26.34, "wall_s": 11.8, "text": "\n\n<think>\nThe user wants me to continue the text with a detailed, new paragraph about how these records are audited. The text above is a collection of repeated sentences about various topics (logistics reconciliation, tidal gauges, maintenance protocols, cooperative bylaws, archival records, firmware changelogs). I need to write a new paragraph about how these records are audited, connecting the themes mentioned in the text.\n\nLet me write a detailed, coherent paragraph about auditing these records, tying together the various themes mentioned: logistics ledgers, customs declarations, tidal gauge recalibrations, maintenance protocols, cooperative bylaws, archival parcel records, and firmware changelogs.\n</think>\n\nThese records are audited through a layered verification framework that begins with a cross-institutional data integrity review, in which the logistics ledger entries are matched against customs declarations, parcel renumbering logs, and firmware changelogs to confirm that no identifier has been duplicated, omitted, or misaligned across systems. Auditors first establish a baseline by pulling the original bill-of-lading identifiers from the shipping manifests and comparing them against the customs filings timestamped before departure, flagging any discrepancies in sequence numbers, cargo descriptions, or declared weights. Simultaneously, the maintenance records are subjected to a compliance audit that checks whether the torque sequences and thermal tolerance readings logged during each inspection cycle fall within the manufacturer's specified ranges, and whether the operating-hour-based inspection intervals were honored rather than deferred to calendar-based scheduling. The tidal gauge recalibration data is then traced back to the dredging permit and the original datum reference to verify that every subsequent flood model used the corrected datum rather than the pre-dredging baseline, a step that requires the auditor to reconcile the survey office's parcel renumbering records with the tax rolls and deeds to ensure that the geographic coordinates tied to each gauge station remained consistent across both renumbering events. For"}, {"depth": 32793, "prompt_n": 32793, "prefill_tps": 1108.5, "decode_tps": 38.77, "decode_ms": 25.79, "wall_s": 39.7, "text": "\n\n<think>\nThe user wants me to continue the text with a detailed, new paragraph about how these records are audited. The text above is a repetitive collection of sentences about various topics (logistics ledger reconciliation, tidal gauges, maintenance protocols, cooperative bylaws, archival records, firmware changelogs). I need to write a new, coherent paragraph about how these records are audited, drawing on the themes present in the text.\n\nLet me write a detailed paragraph about auditing these records, connecting the various themes mentioned (logistics ledgers, customs declarations, tidal gauge data, maintenance protocols, cooperative bylaws, archival records, firmware changelogs).\n</think>\n\nThe audit of these records follows a layered protocol that begins with a cross-verification of the logistics ledger against the customs declarations, ensuring that every bill-of-lading identifier maps to a filed declaration before the vessel's departure window closes. Auditors then trace the tidal gauge recalibration logs to confirm that the datum shift introduced by the dredging operation was properly propagated into all subsequent flood models, flagging any model that still references the pre-dredging datum as a compliance exception. For the maintenance protocols, the audit team checks whether inspection intervals were recorded against cumulative operating hours rather than calendar dates, pulling sensor telemetry from the torque wrenches and thermal probes to validate that no unit exceeded its rated tolerance between inspections. The cooperative's financial records are examined against the harvest-cycle deferral schedule, with auditors reconciling deferred dues against the autumn cash-flow peak and the spring trough to ensure no member's obligation was silently extinguished. Archival parcel records undergo a forensic renumbering audit, where the survey office's two renumbering events are mapped against both the tax rolls and the deed registry to identify orphaned parcels that appear in one dataset but not the other. Finally, the firmware changelog entries are subjected to a regression audit, in which"}, {"depth": 134029, "prompt_n": 103288, "prefill_tps": 723.8, "decode_tps": 32.0, "decode_ms": 31.25, "wall_s": 154.9, "text": "\n\n<think>\nThe user has provided a very long text that consists of repeated sentences about various topics (logistics ledger reconciliation, tidal gauges, maintenance protocols, cooperative bylaws, archival records, firmware changelogs). They want me to continue the text with a detailed, new paragraph about how these records are audited.\n\nLet me write a coherent, detailed paragraph about the auditing process for these various records. I should make it relevant to the topics mentioned in the text - logistics ledgers, customs declarations, tidal gauge recalibrations, maintenance protocols, cooperative bylaws, archival parcel records, and firmware changelogs.\n\nI'll write a substantive paragraph that ties together the auditing of these diverse records.\n</think>\n\nThe audit of these records follows a layered protocol that begins with a cross-referential integrity check, in which the logistics ledger entries are matched against the bill-of-lading identifiers and the customs declarations filed before departure, ensuring that no shipment is recorded without a corresponding regulatory filing and that no declaration exists without a traceable cargo manifest. Auditors then examine the tidal gauge recalibration logs to verify that the datum shift introduced by the dredging operation was properly propagated into every subsequent flood model, flagging any model that still references the pre-dredging datum as a potential source of downstream error. Maintenance records are scrutinized against the operating-hour counters rather than calendar dates, since the inspection interval is tied to cumulative runtime; auditors pull the torque-sequence logs and thermal-tolerance readings from the equipment's embedded telemetry to confirm that each inspection occurred within the prescribed hour window and that no thermal excursion exceeded the documented tolerance band. For the cooperative's financial records, the audit traces deferred dues through the harvest season into the autumn cash-flow peak, reconciling member deferrals against the spring trough to ensure that no deferred obligation was silently written off or double-counted. The archival parcel renumbering presents"}, {"depth": 250712, "prompt_n": 118735, "prefill_tps": 443.4, "decode_tps": 30.18, "decode_ms": 33.14, "wall_s": 280.9, "text": "\n\n<think>\nThe user has provided a very long text that consists of repeated sentences about various topics (logistics ledger reconciliation, tidal gauges, maintenance protocols, cooperative bylaws, archival records, firmware changelogs). They want me to continue the text with a detailed, new paragraph about how these records are audited.\n\nLet me write a coherent, detailed paragraph about the auditing process for these various types of records. I should make it relevant to the topics mentioned in the text - logistics ledgers, customs declarations, tidal gauge data, maintenance protocols, cooperative financial records, archival parcel records, and firmware changelogs.\n\nI'll write a substantive paragraph that addresses how these diverse records are audited, tying together the themes present in the text.\n</think>\n\nThe auditing of these records follows a layered protocol that begins with automated cross-validation scripts run against the logistics ledger, where bill-of-lading identifiers are matched line-by-line against the customs declarations filed prior to departure, flagging any discrepancies in shipment volume, destination codes, or timestamp alignment for manual review by a certified customs compliance officer. Tidal gauge recalibration logs are audited by comparing the pre-dredging datum readings against the post-dredging baseline using a certified metrology laboratory's traceability chain, ensuring that every subsequent flood model references the corrected datum rather than the obsolete one; the calibration certificates are retained for a minimum of ten years and are subject to spot-checks by the national hydrographic authority. Maintenance protocol compliance is verified through a dual-track audit: the torque-sequence and thermal-tolerance entries are sampled against the equipment's electronic service history, while the inspection-interval records\u2014tied to cumulative operating hours rather than calendar dates\u2014are reconciled against the machine's runtime telemetry to confirm that no unit has exceeded its service window without a logged intervention. Cooperative financial records are audited annually by an independent chartered accountant who traces"}], "log": "$BENCH/W9-L-llamacpp-r1-20260927-113415.log"}
